  "security_implications": "The wipe_secret signal controls a secret key wipe operation (directly driven by a CSR qualified event). If the CSR event is missed, glitched, or not latched correctly, the wipe may be incomplete or omitted, leaving sensitive key material in registers. The err_valid suppression mechanism (using reg2hw.intr_state.hmac_err.q) may mask new errors if the interrupt is already pending, potentially hiding security-relevant error conditions such as an invalid configuration or a forbidden operation during an active hash. The key_length_supplied signal directly reflects a CSR field and is used in key handling; an incorrect cast or misinterpretation could lead to wrong key length processing, compromising HMAC integrity.",
